# Search-scope hints for ripgrep and the tools built on it (rg, the Grep/Glob
# tools of Claude Code and OpenCode, many editors). This is NOT a git ignore:
# everything listed here stays tracked and buildable. It only keeps default,
# repo-wide searches from drowning in content that is never the answer for
# work in this fork (see AGENTS.md, "Context economy").
#
# To search an excluded path anyway:
#   rg --no-ignore-dot <pattern>             # ignore this file, keep .gitignore
#   rg <pattern> thirdparty/vulkan          # explicit path works as well
#
# Keep the list short and justified. Each entry must be either large, generated,
# or explicitly not a source of truth.

# Upstream translations: ~60 MB of .po files; every English word matches.
/doc/translations/
/editor/translations/

# Vendored third-party code (4.5k files). Search it by explicit path when you
# really need a vendored header.
/thirdparty/

# Huge single-file scene (60 MB of text in 239 lines) and binary splat caches.
/tests/examples/godot/test_project/scenes/lighting_test.tscn
*.gsplatcache

# Generated or archived reports and data dumps, not sources of truth.
/docs/reports/
/docs/assets/data/
/docs/architecture/generated/

# Legacy coordination memory. AGENTS.md: "Not source of truth".
/docs/agent_memory/

# Local-only material that may exist in a developer checkout (untracked).
/exhibition/
/HANDOFF_*.md
/STATS.md
/issues.json
/.claude/worktrees/
